  "summary": "The Santa Clara County Board of Supervisors voted to stop using Flock Safety as its ALPR vendor in Cupertino, Saratoga, and Los Altos Hills, which are policed by the county sheriff. The decision followed revelations that federal agencies had accessed Flock camera data in Mountain View without consent.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Santa Clara County will no longer use Flock Safety as the primary vendor for their license plate readers in Cupertino, Saratoga and Los Altos Hills after a vote by the Board of Supervisors",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Mass surveillance does not keep our public safe, but endangers all of us",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock has gone on the record publicly that it does not have any contracts with ICE or CBP... Only our customers have sole authority over if, when, and with whom information is shared.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
